# ==============================================================================
# Example 49: Synechocystis sp. PCC 6803 — Freshwater Cyanobacteria
# ==============================================================================
#
# Organism: Synechocystis sp. PCC 6803 (cyanobacterium)
# Genome: NCBI RefSeq NC_020286.1 (3,573,470 bp, circular chromosome)
# Environment: Freshwater lake surface (photic zone, 25°C, 12h light/12h dark)
#
# Synechocystis is a model photosynthetic prokaryote — the "E. coli of
# cyanobacteria." It performs oxygenic photosynthesis, fixes CO₂ via the
# Calvin cycle, and exhibits a robust circadian clock (~24h rhythm).
# Unlike E. coli, it cannot use glucose as a sole carbon source under
# normal conditions; instead it captures light energy and fixes inorganic
# carbon (CO₂/HCO₃⁻).
#
# Life activities modeled:
#   1. Photosystem I  — psaA: P700 reaction center (light-driven electron transport)
#   2. Photosystem II — psbA: D1 protein (water-splitting, O₂ evolution)
#   3. Carbon fixation — rbcL: RuBisCO large subunit (Calvin cycle)
#   4. Light harvesting — cpcB: Phycocyanin β-chain (accessory pigment)
#   5. Circadian clock — kaiA: KaiA oscillator (24h transcription-translation feedback)
#   6. NDH-1 complex  — ndhB: NAD(P)H dehydrogenase (cyclic electron flow, CO₂ uptake)
#   7. Stress response — groEL: Chaperonin (protein folding under high-light / heat)
#
# Gene sequences: real Synechocystis sp. PCC 6803 proteins from NCBI Protein
# database (WP_014407086, CAR8497204, Q55875, CAR8496286, P72714, CAR8480292),
# back-translated to Synechocystis codon-optimized DNA.
#
# Growth environment:
#   Light intensity: 200 µmol photons/m²/s (photon flux density)
#   CO₂: 0.04% (atmospheric)
#   Temperature: 25°C (optimal for Synechocystis)
#   Medium: BG-11 (freshwater cyanobacteria growth medium)
#
# Expected behavior:
#   Day phase (light on):  photosynthesis active, O₂ evolution, CO₂ fixation,
#                           glycogen storage, circadian gate open
#   Night phase (light off): respiration dominant, glycogen consumption,
#                             circadian gate closed, D1 repair cycle
# ==============================================================================

#gem organism=synechocystis_pcc6803 medium=bg11 use_database=true include_spontaneous=true gapfill=true dynamic=true duration=48.0 dt=0.05 expression=true target_organism=Synechocystis_sp_PCC_6803

